---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import ComingSoon from '../../components/ComingSoon.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Retail — Use Case"
  description="Queue analytics and shelf monitoring in plain English — no per-store model training required."
  canonicalPath="/use-cases/retail"
  mdTwin="/use-cases/retail.md"
>
  <div class="page">
    <a class="back" href="/use-cases">← Use cases</a>
    <section class="hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">Retail</p>
      <h1>Queue analytics and shelf monitoring in plain English</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        No per-store model training. Just ask.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="content">
      <p>
        Retail environments vary enormously: store layouts change, lighting conditions shift,
        camera angles differ by location. Traditional CV pipelines require per-store training
        runs each time any of those variables change — a labeling and retraining budget that
        scales with your store count, not your revenue. Primate Vision asks the question in
        plain English and gets a deterministic answer, regardless of the camera or the store.
      </p>
      <p>
        Queue analytics: "How many people are waiting at checkout?" Shelf monitoring:
        "Is the end-cap display stocked?" Loss prevention: "Did anyone place merchandise in
        a bag without scanning it?" Each of these is a prompt, not a model. Change the
        question without changing the infrastructure. The outputs are timestamped and
        structured — usable as signals in your existing operations dashboard or BI stack.
      </p>

      <ComingSoon note="Retail deployment guide and example prompts — coming during our August launch." />
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .page { max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 64px 24px 96px; }
  .back { font-size: 14px; color: var(--color-text-muted); display: block; margin-bottom: 32px; }
  .back:hover { color: var(--color-signal); }
  .hero { margin-bottom: 40px; }
  .eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 500;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--color-signal);
    margin: 0 0 12px;
  }
  h1 { font-size: 44px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.02em; line-height: 1.2; margin: 0 0 16px; }
  .lede { font-size: 18px; color: var(--color-text-muted); line-height: 1.6; margin: 0; }
  .content p { font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.75; color: var(--color-text-primary); opacity: 0.85; margin: 0 0 16px; }
  @media (max-width: 640px) { h1 { font-size: 32px; } .page { padding: 44px 20px 64px; } }
</style>
